{"kind":"assert","text":"Trace of `dap verify \u003clane\u003e` for 9f80a194. This needs your ruling, because the fix I see reverses a position the tests pin.\n\n**Cause.** The refused scope `sc_hdhtyut3...` is another room's directory. Rita's room shares a register with 12 rooms, and the first of them founded at register entries 1 to 3. A lane's proof replays the register up to its own room's creation, entries 0 to 33 here. Register entry 3 is a result delivery from that other directory's entry 0, and the verifier must prove the source of each delivery (`packages/replay/src/verify.ts:2029-2034`, stop at `:1557`). The CLI words it at `packages/cli/src/commands.ts:760-767`.\n\n**The read.** Observed in a rerun on dap-demo from Rita's home and Una's home: `GET .../sc_hdhtyut3.../log` answers 403 forbidden, both with the session and with a signed read. From source only: a directory admits only its own room's membership (`packages/scope/src/sessions.ts:256-258`), and the register alone admits other rooms' sessions (`reads.ts:125-131`, decision `ca8ad1cf`). So no grant exists to give. Being an admin does not help.\n\n**Who it hits.** Observed in this room: the lane, the membership, the directory and each `--all` line inspected. From source: every room on a shared register except the first. Tests pass because `apps/room/lanes/test/issues.scope.test.ts:176` runs one room on its register. `packages/cli/test/claim.scope.test.ts:425-430` and `verify.test.ts:177` pin the refusal as the expected words, by f256c652.\n\n**Options.**\n1. Anchor other rooms' results. The CLI takes each register result whose source directory is not this room's, and passes it to the verifier as an anchor (`commands.ts:827`, `:926` for `--all`). The report lists each one as taken on the caller's word. A read-only scratch run with Una's session on this lane returned `consistent`: 24 foreign facts replayed, 10 anchored, 0 missing, with coverage lane 0 to 12, own directory 0 to 6, register 0 to 33. The anchored `--all` path has not run.\n2. Let the Worker serve a foreign directory's genesis entry to a register reader. Nothing is taken on trust, but this widens read access across rooms.\n3. Keep the refusal and change the words, so that a person learns the lane itself is not in doubt. The person still cannot verify.\n\n**My recommendation: option 1.** It keeps each room's reads closed, and the report says plainly what it trusts: other rooms' creation results, which do not change this room's state. The result reads `consistent` with a stated trust, so it claims less than a first room's full replay. Option 1 flips the two pinned tests, and a new test runs `verify` on a second room's directory.\n\nThe question: which option do you rule? I hold 9f80a194 unpromised until you do, and I continue the Page change meanwhile.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}